<!--
  Adaptive icon foreground: a four-point cross sparkle, the same mark as
  AppGlyphs.sparkle (flutter/lib/ui/glyphs.dart) but filled solid instead of
  stroked.

  Why this construction:
  - Tips stay on the axes (up / right / down / left) so it reads as a cross
    sparkle, not a diamond or the old eight-petal starburst.
  - The glyph's straight inner edges are replaced by cubic curves: the waist
    is a smooth tangent join (r = 9), while short 4.2-unit handles keep the
    tips sharp. The waist is slightly fatter than the 24-unit glyph (r/R 0.35
    vs 0.30) so the solid fill still has body at 48dp.
  - A small companion star (R = 5.6) in the upper-right notch adds the
    "sparkle" read and a second layer of depth without a second color.
    Its farthest tip sits at r = 27.3 from center, inside the 33dp safe
    circle; the main star tops out at R = 26.
  Canvas is the standard 108x108 adaptive-icon viewport.
-->
